# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the window-WY probe's card step (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of the integration branch and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN (the tag numbers are the driver's, on the
# allowlist). Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the card is resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch.
# NON-EXACT RESEARCH PROBE (docs/gdn-wy-probe.md): no verdict of this job licenses serving, and the window form is never in a serving or traffic profile.
# ONE IMAGE: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-wy-probe-1 is a PLACEHOLDER the driver substitutes with the combined window's fresh tag; the harness mounts this checkout's scripts, so any
# current C2 image carries the runtime it needs and no build is specific to this probe.
# W2: the full window-WY probe on one card. Sections: selftest, sram (circular-buffer bytes against L1), causality (n = 1, 4, 8, 15, 16, 17, 24, 31 rows committed of a 32-row block, rows 0..n-1
# and the committed state as raw bytes, later rows real / zero / other, NaN informational, K5-A control and a changed-earlier-row control), packing (the four-user launch against four
# one-user launches, byte for byte), accuracy (the CORRECTNESS GATE: W's outputs and committed states for both windows against the fp64 reference, within 1.5x K5-A's own error) and timing (A, A2, W1, W2 in one trace of 48 launches, 25 serpentine rounds).
# KILL rules (exit 10): two windows in one launch above 90 us a layer (at the full timing scope only), any causality mismatch, any packing mismatch, W outside 1.5x K5-A's error against fp64, circular buffers over L1, an unwritten page or an input that moved.
# REQUIRES-FILE scripts/ci/gdn_wy_block.py; the driver SKIPS this job unless the integration commit holds that file (without it the run is W0's baseline and ends NO-DECISION).
# CONTINUE (exit 0) means only that every kill rule held at full scope: it is the owner's decision whether to start the programme, never a serving licence.
# Duration (estimate): 45-60 min (219 launches in the full plan, 220 input read-backs; container timeout 2 h, twice the estimate; the per-call watchdog exits 3 on a hang, then reset the target card only).
# Read: 'GDN_WY verdict=... scope=full kernel=present ...' and the last JSON line (timing: a_us, a2_us, w1_us, w2_us, speedup_vs_a2). STOP on KILL (exit 10) or NO-DECISION (exit 4).
C2_CARDS=pair
C2_ACTIONS=cardm
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-wy-probe-1
C2_CARDM_HARNESS=optimisation/ttnn-op/wy_probe/run_card_m.sh
C2_CARDM_ENV=IMAGE_TAG=tp4-wy-probe-1
